# Sticker System

> Backend API is NOT ready yet. The frontend foundation is in place for when the server adds sticker support.

## Architecture

```
entities/sticker/
├── sticker.types.ts      ← Sticker, StickerPack, StickerFormat, API contracts
├── sticker.model.ts      ← Zustand store: packs, recent, favorites, search
├── sticker.api.ts        ← API stubs + markdown helpers (build/parse/detect)
└── index.ts              ← Public barrel

features/sticker-picker/
├── sticker-picker.ui.tsx ← Telegram-style picker panel (search, pack tabs, grid)
└── index.ts

shared/ui/
└── sticker-message.tsx   ← Renders sticker in message bubble
```

## Message Format

Stickers are sent as regular Zulip messages with a special markdown format:

```
[sticker:pack_id:sticker_id](https://cdn.example.com/stickers/pack/sticker.webp)
```

This degrades gracefully in clients without sticker support — they see a linked image.

### Helpers

```ts
import {
  buildStickerMarkdown,   // Sticker → markdown string
  parseStickerFromContent, // markdown → { packId, stickerId, url } | null
  isStickerMessage,        // is content a sticker-only message?
} from "~/entities/sticker";
```

## Store (useStickerStore)

```ts
import { useStickerStore } from "~/entities/sticker";

// Read
const packs = useStickerStore(s => s.packs);
const sticker = useStickerStore(s => s.getSticker("s1"));
const results = useStickerStore(s => s.searchByEmoji("👍"));
const recent = useStickerStore(s => s.getRecentStickers());
const favs = useStickerStore(s => s.getFavoriteStickers());

// Write
useStickerStore.getState().setPacks(packsFromApi);
useStickerStore.getState().addPack(newPack);
useStickerStore.getState().removePack("p1");
useStickerStore.getState().addRecent("s1", "p1");
useStickerStore.getState().toggleFavorite("s1");
```

Recent (up to 30) and favorites (up to 50) persist in localStorage.

## Sticker Formats

| Format | Extension | Rendering | Status |
|--------|-----------|-----------|--------|
| `webp` | `.webp` | `<img>` | Ready |
| `png` | `.png` | `<img>` | Ready |
| `lottie` | `.json` / `.tgs` | `lottie-web` (future) | Placeholder |
| `webm` | `.webm` | `<video>` (future) | Placeholder |

## StickerPicker (UI)

```tsx
import { StickerPicker } from "~/features/sticker-picker";

<StickerPicker
  onSelect={(sticker) => {
    const md = buildStickerMarkdown(sticker);
    sendMessage({ content: md, stream, subject });
  }}
  onClose={() => setPickerOpen(false)}
/>
```

Layout:
1. Search bar (filters by emoji / alt text)
2. Pack tabs (horizontal scroll, cover sticker as icon, Recent tab)
3. Sticker grid (4 columns, lazy-loaded thumbnails)

## StickerMessage (Rendering)

```tsx
import { shouldRenderAsSticker, StickerMessage } from "~/shared/ui";

// In MessageBubble:
if (shouldRenderAsSticker(message.content)) {
  return <StickerMessage content={message.content} maxSize={180} />;
}
```

Sticker-only messages render without the message bubble background (larger, standalone).
Mixed content messages render the sticker inline (smaller).

## When Backend is Ready

Replace stubs in `sticker.api.ts`:

1. `fetchStickerPacks()` → `GET /sticker-packs`
2. `fetchStickerPack(id)` → `GET /sticker-packs/{id}`
3. `installStickerPack(id)` → `POST /sticker-packs/{id}/install`
4. `uninstallStickerPack(id)` → `DELETE /sticker-packs/{id}/install`
5. `searchStickers(query)` → `GET /stickers/search?q=...`

Add event loop handler for `sticker_pack` events (new pack available, pack updated).

## Rules for AI Agent

### When implementing sticker features

1. **Sticker = regular message** — use `buildStickerMarkdown()`, send via normal `sendMessage()`
2. **Detection** — use `isStickerMessage()` / `parseStickerFromContent()` to identify stickers
3. **Rendering** — use `<StickerMessage>` in message bubble; switch rendering mode via `shouldRenderAsSticker()`
4. **Store** — all sticker state lives in `useStickerStore`; no ad-hoc state
5. **Formats** — WebP/PNG now, Lottie/WebM as future extensions
6. **Accessibility** — every sticker needs `alt` text (emoji or description)

### Do NOT

- Do NOT send sticker files as regular file uploads — use the markdown format
- Do NOT store full sticker images in localStorage — only IDs and metadata
- Do NOT hardcode sticker URLs — they come from the API/pack data
- Do NOT block on backend — all API functions are stubbed and return empty results
